(D3 - Discrepancy 3 repro: a float operand makes every bitwise
 operator return 0.0 silently. 3.5 truncated to 3 would give 3 bit-and
 1 = 1; 6.0 truncated to 6 would give 6 bit-and 4 = 4. Both give 0.0,
 and the result keeps float type. A text or list operand in the same
 position is a clean compile error (OPR-42), so the float case is the
 one operand type that is neither converted nor refused.
